{"name":"American Beauty","hex":"#a73340","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"American Beauty","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep pink to crimson rose cultivar, bred by Henri Lédéchaux in France in 1875."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/American_Beauty"}],"entries":[{"title":"American Beauty (Ferber novel)","blocks":[{"text":"American Beauty is a 1931 novel by American author Edna Ferber first published by Doubleday Doran. Set in the Housatonic region of Connecticut, the story, spanning from the year 1700 to 1930, relates the steady decline of the Oakes family and their property, as well as their tense relations with Polish immigrants."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b6/AmericanBeautyFerber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Beauty_(Ferber_novel)","wikidata":"Q4743157"},{"title":"American Beauty (Dean novel)","blocks":[{"text":"American Beauty is the seventh novel in the A-List series by Zoey Dean. It was released in 2006 through Megan Tingley Publishers."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2d/Zoey_Dean_-_The_A-List_7_American_Beauty_An_A-List_Novel.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Beauty_(Dean_novel)","wikidata":"Q4743158"},{"title":"American Beauty (1999 film)","blocks":[{"text":"American Beauty is a 1999 American black comedy and psychological drama film directed by Sam Mendes in his feature-film directorial debut, and written by Alan Ball. Kevin Spacey stars as Lester Burnham, an advertising executive who experiences a midlife crisis after becoming infatuated with his daughter’s teenage best friend, played by Mena Suvari. Annette Bening stars as Lester's materialistic wife, Carolyn, and Thora Birch plays their insecure daughter, Jane. Wes Bentley, Chris Cooper, Peter Gallagher, and Allison Janney co-star."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9a/American_Beauty_1999_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Beauty_(1999_film)","wikidata":"Q25139"},{"title":"Beauty","blocks":[{"text":"Beauty is commonly described as a feature of objects that makes them pleasurable to perceive. Such objects include landscapes, sunsets, humans and works of art. Beauty, art and taste are the main subjects of aesthetics, one of the fields of study within philosophy. As a positive aesthetic value, it is contrasted with ugliness as its negative counterpart."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Rozeta_Pary%C5%BC_notre-dame_chalger.jpg/330px-Rozeta_Pary%C5%BC_notre-dame_chalger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beauty","wikidata":"Q7242"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d8/American_Beauty_jail_cell.png/330px-American_Beauty_jail_cell.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d8/American_Beauty_jail_cell.png/330px-American_Beauty_jail_cell.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" The theme of imprisonment is evoked in this scene showing Lester's reflection in the monitor behind columns of data, which resembles an inmate in a jail cell.[8][9]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmerican_Beauty_jail_cell.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Principal_cast_of_American_Beauty.jpg/500px-Principal_cast_of_American_Beauty.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Principal_cast_of_American_Beauty.jpg/500px-Principal_cast_of_American_Beauty.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The principal actors and actressesFirst row: Wes Bentley, Chris Cooper, Mena Suvari, Kevin SpaceySecond row: Annette Bening, Thora Birch, Allison Janney","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APrincipal_cast_of_American_Beauty.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Aerial_view_of_Sacramento.jpg/500px-Aerial_view_of_Sacramento.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Aerial_view_of_Sacramento.jpg/1280px-Aerial_view_of_Sacramento.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Aerial_view_of_Sacramento.jpg/500px-Aerial_view_of_Sacramento.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The film used aerial shots of Sacramento, California, at the beginning and end of the film to show where the Burnhams live.[126]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAerial_view_of_Sacramento.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/American_Beauty_theater_count.png/500px-American_Beauty_theater_count.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/American_Beauty_theater_count.png/1280px-American_Beauty_theater_count.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/American_Beauty_theater_count.png/500px-American_Beauty_theater_count.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Graph showing the number of theaters in which American Beauty played in North America in 1999–2000. After the film's Golden Globe success in January 2000, DreamWorks re-expanded its market presence to 1,990 theaters.[15